              "type": "Type"
            }
          ],
          "content": "Rembrandt drew this little house on the Spaarndammerdijk during one of his walks around Amsterdam. The drawing served as the starting point for the 1648 etching. There are a number of differences between the drawing and the print. The etching is much smaller, the trees have a completely different shape, and Rembrandt added various objects to it, such as a horse’s skull."
        },
        {
          "type": "LinguisticObject",
          "classified_as": [
            {
